ut 9 units short per two-day cycle. At 1.2× it runs about 3 short. Over 15 cycles that gap is worth hundreds of points, which drops candidate 4 out of the top group.\n   - Candidate 3 orders every 3 days but covers product 1 at about 1.2×. That should put it ahead of candidates 4, 5 and 6.\n   - Candidate 6 orders daily at only about 1.05–1.1× and has no pooling buffer, so it faces more shortages.\n\n3. **Risk.** All plans face the same early shortage of product 1, since the starting 60 units can't cover days 0–4 before the first delivery. That doesn't separate them. When demand differs from the forecast, the plans with more buffer (2, 0) hold up best.\n\nCandidates 2, 0 and 7 are my firm picks. The fourth slot, candidate 3 against candidate 4, is the least certain call."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5042, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5042}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:19:54.511Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWCbf7sbbvB3UVTGVgk5"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01GERdbju64aAjFD4hXZ9d4D", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWCbfUTUUkzF73niFnAt", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01GERdbju64aAjFD4hXZ9d4D", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.75, 0.15, 0.75, 0.5, 0.4, 0.